## 9. Ongoing Monitoring Plan

**Current baseline:** {{ pooled_tuning.avg_alerts_per_month }} alerts/month and a {{ pooled_tuning.productive }} productive rate in the tuning period; {{ pooled_validation.avg_alerts_per_month }} alerts/month and {{ pooled_validation.productive }} in validation.

- **Alert volume drift:** investigate if a future month's volume for this scenario deviates by more than 50% from the {{ pooled_tuning.avg_alerts_per_month }}/month tuning-period baseline, or approaches the {{ pooled_capacity }}/month capacity ceiling.
- **Productive rate drift:** investigate if the productive rate over a rolling 2-month window falls below half of the validation-period level ({{ pooled_validation.productive }}).
- **Re-tuning triggers:** re-run Phase 5 tuning (a) on a fixed cadence as new labeled cases accumulate, (b) immediately if a segment's labeled case count crosses the {{ capacity_cfg.min_tuning_cases_for_segment_specific_threshold }}-tuning-case / 1-validation-case threshold used for the segment-specific-vs-pooled decision in Section 5, or (c) if either drift condition above persists for two consecutive months.

